over the past few years billions have  been invested in an industry that  promised to rival pro sports leagues but  now the Esports organizations who sought  to pave this future face a tough  Reckoning is the dream of Esports  already dying  [Music]  Giants of the Space Team Solomid and 100  thieves have terminated dozens of  positions between them others who own  teams in supposedly lucrative leagues  have sold to third parties The  consultancy Firm Deloitte expects only  about a third of European Esports teams  to turn a profit this year money seems  to be much harder to come by the problem  is that Esports teams are dependent on  Advertising they had hoped to fill  stadiums with screaming fans and secure  lucrative broadcast deals but those have  largely failed to materialize lately  about 60 percent of their revenue still  comes from advertising and sponsorships  and when the global economy slows ad  budgets are usually the first to be cut  what's more many of the advertisers were  crypto companies who've been having  their own tough time FTX the bankrupt  crypto exchange had pledged 210 million  dollars for team Solomid to change its  name to TSM FTX the deal is now on hold  finally venture capitalist interest is  cooled back in 2018 they invested about  three times more in Esports than this  year and are less willing to cover  losses much of the hype previously  dedicated to Esports is moving over to  gaming influencers who live stream  themselves on Twitch and YouTube the  cash crunch has left a slew of teams  fighting to ensure it's not game over
 

